{"test":{"id":1722,"name":"B5.b catalog tri-mirror contract documents grant intent and MFA posture","suiteID":1583,"groupIDs":[1719,1720],"metadata":{"skip":false,"skipReason":null},"line":38,"column":5,"url":"file:///C:/Git%20Local%20Repos/forge_flow_demo/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5ebc703d1ba5735f/test/auth/permission_catalog_b5b_test.dart"},"type":"testStart","time":114475}
{"testID":1722,"error":"Expected: contains '`operator_owner` and `operator_admin`'\n  Actual: '# Auth Permission Key Catalog\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '**Status:** Active. Lands with Phase 9.0.\\r\\n'\n            '**Authority order:** This contract documents the frozen catalog. The\\r\\n'\n            'canonical sources are the SQL seed in\\r\\n'\n            '`db/migrations/202604250008_auth_schema_foundation.sql`, additive catalog\\r\\n'\n            'migrations in `db/migrations/`, and the constants in\\r\\n'\n            '`lib/auth/permission_keys.dart`. This doc must stay in sync with those.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '## Why a frozen catalog\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Permission keys are app-defined. Operators may not invent new keys at\\r\\n'\n            'runtime. Custom roles introduced via the 9.6 admin endpoints choose\\r\\n'\n            'which existing keys they grant or deny — they cannot extend the\\r\\n'\n            'universe of keys. Freezing the catalog at code level keeps:\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '- Permission resolution deterministic across the proxy + Flutter\\r\\n'\n            '  surfaces.\\r\\n'\n            '- The audit trail (`role_audit_log`, `auth_events_audit`) intelligible\\r\\n'\n            '  to F&F support and ops.\\r\\n'\n            '- The MFA-required set (`requires_mfa = true`) auditable: changing it\\r\\n'\n            '  requires a code change + migration, not a runtime row update.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '## Keep in sync\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'When adding, renaming, or removing a key, update all three together:\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '1. `db/migrations/` - either the foundation `insert into\\r\\n'\n            '   public.permission_keys` block or an additive follow-up migration.\\r\\n'\n            '2. `lib/auth/permission_keys.dart` — add the constant + add to\\r\\n'\n            '   `PermissionKeys.all` (and `requiresMfa` if applicable).\\r\\n'\n            '3. This document — add the row to the table for the right category.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'The 9.0 test group (`Phase 9 auth schema foundation migration (9.0)`)\\r\\n'\n            'in `test/advisor_proxy_test.dart` asserts that the migration seeds at\\r\\n'\n            'least the keys exposed by `PermissionKeys.all`; if you add a key in\\r\\n'\n            'the constants without seeding it, the test catches that.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '## Categories\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'The catalog carries 84 keys across 7 categories in the core catalog\\r\\n'\n            '(81 original + 2 admin keys added after baseline +\\r\\n'\n            '`admin.users.reset_mfa_factors` added in 11A.14). The 14 `team.*` keys\\r\\n'\n            'added across 9.0a, the MFA hardening slice, and 11W.5 live in their own\\r\\n'\n            'section below; the Phase 8.0 single `integrations.configure` key adds a\\r\\n'\n            '9th category. B5.b adds `account.*` and `business_timing.*` settings\\r\\n'\n            'categories. The running total across all 11 categories is 103 keys.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '### `product.*` (2)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Product-shell access gates. A user without the matching `product.*`\\r\\n'\n            'key cannot enter the product shell at all. `product.forgeflow.access`\\r\\n'\n            'is required for both standalone Forge & Flow and the Forge & Flow\\r\\n'\n            'surfaces inside Barrio. `product.barrio.access` is required for\\r\\n'\n            'Barrio surfaces. The Barrio admin pattern (Hard Promise: superset)\\r\\n'\n            'holds both.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Key | Description | MFA |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `product.forgeflow.access` | Access to Forge & Flow surfaces in either product shell. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `product.barrio.access` | Access to Barrio surfaces in the Barrio product shell. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '### `forgeflow.*` (20)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Forge & Flow surface views and actions. Splitting `view` from `edit`\\r\\n'\n            'allows the Phase 9 RBAC plan to seat read-only operators\\r\\n'\n            '(`supervisor`) below editors (`location_manager`,\\r\\n'\n            '`operator_general_manager`, `operator_owner`). (Pre-v2 wording named\\r\\n'\n            'the retired `operator_supervisor` / `operator_manager` roles here;\\r\\n'\n            'see \"Baseline Roles (seeded)\" for the v1→v2 mapping.)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Key | Description | MFA |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.shift.view` | View shift surface. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.shift.edit` | Edit shift assignments. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.variance.view` | View variance surface. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.variance.edit` | Edit variance reasons and notes. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.schedule.view` | View schedule surface. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.schedule.edit` | Edit upcoming schedule assignments. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.baseline.view` | View baseline benchmark. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.baseline.override` | Override baseline values for a service period. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.history.view` | View historical service-period results. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.benchmark.view` | View 60-day benchmark snapshot. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.benchmark.edit` | Edit 60-day benchmark snapshot inputs. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.target_profile.view` | View active target profile. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.target_profile.manage` | Manage target-profile parameters. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.target_cycle.view` | View target cycle. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.target_cycle.unlock` | Unlock the active target cycle for early replacement. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.target_cycle.replace` | Replace the active target cycle. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.weekly_plan.view` | View locked weekly plan snapshot. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.weekly_plan.lock` | Lock the in-force weekly plan snapshot. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.settings.view` | View Forge & Flow settings. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `forgeflow.settings.manage` | Manage Forge & Flow settings. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '### `barrio.*` (12)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Barrio learning surfaces. Most are scoped reads; `*.edit` keys exist\\r\\n'\n            'where operator owners or F&F may curate Barrio content per operator.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Key | Description | MFA |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `barrio.handbook.view` | View Barrio handbook. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `barrio.interview_playbook.view` | View interview playbook. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `barrio.jim_taylor.view` | View Jim Taylor course. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `barrio.preston_lee.view` | View Preston Lee course. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `barrio.supervisor_content.view` | View supervisor learning content. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `barrio.el_podio.view` | View El Podio leaderboard surfaces. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `barrio.handbook.edit` | Edit Barrio handbook content (operator owner / F&F only). | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `barrio.interview_playbook.edit` | Edit interview-playbook content. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `barrio.preston_lee.edit` | Edit Preston Lee course content. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `barrio.supervisor_content.edit` | Edit supervisor learning content. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `barrio.learning.complete_unit` | Mark a learning unit complete for the current user. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `barrio.streak.view` | View own streak / leaderboard standing. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '### `admin.*` (28)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'F&F admin actions. Mostly mounted under `/v1/admin/auth/*` (9.6, 9.8).\\r\\n'\n            'Sensitive keys carry `requires_mfa = true`. The 9.0Σ.h2 slice\\r\\n'\n            '(2026-04-28) added `admin.audit_privacy.read` to gate the audit-read\\r\\n'\n            'path on `advisor_conversation_log`; that key is seeded by\\r\\n'\n            '`db/migrations/202604280014_phase_9_0sigma_h2_audit_privacy_role.sql`,\\r\\n'\n            'not by the 9.0 foundation seed. The 11A.14 slice (2026-05-06) added\\r\\n'\n            '`admin.users.reset_mfa_factors` to gate the support-side MFA-reset\\r\\n'\n            'escalation; that key is seeded by\\r\\n'\n            '`db/migrations/202605061100_phase_11A_14_admin_users_reset_mfa_factors_key.sql`,\\r\\n'\n            'also not by the 9.0 foundation seed.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Key | Description | MFA |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.users.view` | View users in admin console. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.users.create` | Create users programmatically (rare path). | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.users.deactivate` | Suspend a user account. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.users.reactivate` | Reactivate a suspended user account. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.users.soft_delete` | Soft-delete a user (status -> deleted; data retained). | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.users.erase_pii` | GDPR right-to-erasure: redact PII for a user. Paired-approval + MFA required. | yes |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.users.reset_password` | Trigger admin-initiated password reset for a user. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.users.reset_mfa_factors` | Reset a member\\'s MFA factors from the F&F admin support path. Required for support-side account recovery when the member has lost access to their second factor. Paired with admin_reason on every call. MFA required. | yes |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.invites.create` | Create user invites. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.invites.revoke` | Revoke pending user invites. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.roles.view` | View roles in admin console. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.roles.edit_seeded` | Edit permissions on seeded roles (super_admin only). | yes |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.roles.create_custom` | Create custom operator-scoped roles. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.roles.delete_custom` | Delete custom operator-scoped roles (after revoking grants). | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.roles.assign` | Grant a role to a user. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.roles.revoke` | Revoke a role from a user. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.audit_log.view` | View auth event audit log. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.audit_log.export` | Export audit log to CSV. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.target_cycle.unlock` | Admin-side override of target-cycle lock. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.pricing_tier.view` | View operator pricing tier. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.pricing_tier.edit` | Edit operator pricing tier (F&F super_admin only). | yes |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.feature_flag.view` | View feature flags. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.feature_flag.toggle` | Toggle feature flag value. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.status_page.publish` | Publish a status-page incident or recovery. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.debug_console.view` | View internal debug console. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.session.force_logout` | Force-revoke all sessions for a user. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.service_principal.issue_token` | Issue short-lived service-principal JWTs for automation identities. MFA required. | yes |\\r\\n'\n            '| `admin.audit_privacy.read` | Read raw advisor conversation content (encrypted columns) under the audit-privacy access path. Every call writes an `audit_logs` provenance row capturing reader, reason, target, and records-read count. MFA required. | yes |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '### `team.*` (17)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Operator self-service team management. Distinct from `admin.*` —\\r\\n'\n            '`team.*` keys gate the operator-facing Settings → Team UX (lands in\\r\\n'\n            '9.10) and let an `operator_owner` manage their own users / roles\\r\\n'\n            'without touching F&F-side admin paths.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Added 2026-04-27 by the 9.0a multi-location scale-flow extensions\\r\\n'\n            'slice, with `team.users.reset_mfa` added by the 2026-04-30 MFA\\r\\n'\n            'hardening migration, `team.audit_log.export` added by the 2026-05-06\\r\\n'\n            '11W.5 catalog reconciliation slice, `team.users.self_update` added\\r\\n'\n            'by the 2026-05-14 Wave 2 W-3 self-service profile slice, and the two\\r\\n'\n            '`team.roles.default_catalog.*` keys added by the 2026-05-14 Wave 2\\r\\n'\n            'RP-9 slice for the F&F-internal Default Role Catalog admin surface.\\r\\n'\n            'None require MFA at the catalog level; the launch tier avoids\\r\\n'\n            'mandatory MFA enforcement for admin-tier accounts until post-launch\\r\\n'\n            'stability. The reset-MFA routes still require fresh sign-in through\\r\\n'\n            'route logic because removing a second factor is sensitive.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Key | Description | MFA |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.users.view` | View the operator\\'s user list. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.users.invite` | Create invites for users in own operator. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.users.deactivate` | Suspend a user in own operator. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.users.reactivate` | Reactivate a suspended user. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.users.soft_delete` | Soft-delete a user in own operator. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.users.reset_password` | Admin-initiated password reset for a team member. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.users.reset_mfa` | Start or cancel delayed authenticator-app removal for a team member after fresh authentication. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.users.self_update` | Change your own display name or email from My Account. Distinct from `team.users.invite` which gates editing someone else; every signed-in operator role is granted this key by default. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.roles.view` | View the operator\\'s role list. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.roles.create_custom` | Create operator-scoped custom role. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.roles.assign` | Grant role to user within own operator. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.roles.revoke` | Revoke role from user within own operator. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.roles.default_catalog.view` | View the F&F Default Role Catalog template — read-only access to the seeded role set every new operator begins with. F&F super_admin + ff_support only. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.roles.default_catalog.edit` | Edits the F&F Default Role Catalog template — adds, renames, or removes seeded roles for new operators. F&F super_admin only. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.hierarchy.suspend` | Suspend or reactivate locations and hierarchy levels. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.hierarchy.delete` | Delete locations and empty hierarchy levels. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.audit_log.view` | View audit log scoped to own operator. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.audit_log.export` | View and export team audit log entries (CSV). | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team.session.force_logout` | Force-logout a user\\'s sessions within own operator. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Baseline grants seeded by 9.0a:\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '- `super_admin` gets every key in the catalog. The 9.0 seed grants all\\r\\n'\n            '  original keys, and the 9.0a audit-fix migration grants the later `team.*`\\r\\n'\n            '  keys. The MFA hardening migration grants `team.users.reset_mfa`. The\\r\\n'\n            '  11W.5 reconciliation migration grants `team.audit_log.export`. The\\r\\n'\n            '  W-3 self-service migration grants `team.users.self_update`.\\r\\n'\n            '- `operator_owner` gets ALL `team.*` keys, including\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.users.reset_mfa`, `team.audit_log.export`, hierarchy lifecycle\\r\\n'\n            '  keys, and `team.users.self_update`. This subsumes the audit-log CSV\\r\\n'\n            '  export gate and self-service profile editor that an `operator_admin`\\r\\n'\n            '  tier was previously described as carrying — there is no separate\\r\\n'\n            '  seeded `operator_admin` role; that capability is part of\\r\\n'\n            '  `operator_owner` at launch.\\r\\n'\n            '- `operator_general_manager` (v2; the role formerly described here as\\r\\n'\n            '  `operator_manager`) gets the GM-tier subset:\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.users.view`, `team.users.invite`, `team.users.deactivate`,\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.users.reactivate`, `team.users.reset_password`,\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.users.reset_mfa`, `team.users.self_update`,\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.roles.view`, `team.roles.assign`, `team.roles.revoke`,\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.audit_log.view`. GM **cannot** create custom roles,\\r\\n'\n            '  suspend/delete hierarchy levels, soft-delete users, or export audit\\r\\n'\n            '  logs by default (locked); pulling a full audit trail to CSV is an\\r\\n'\n            '  Owner / Auditor action.\\r\\n'\n            '- `location_manager` (v2 location-scoped) gets `team.users.view`,\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.users.invite`, `team.users.deactivate`, `team.users.self_update`,\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.roles.view`, `team.roles.assign` — all location-scoped via\\r\\n'\n            '  `user_roles.location_id`.\\r\\n'\n            '- `supervisor` (v2; the role the retired `operator_supervisor` /\\r\\n'\n            '  `operator_staff` were auto-migrated into) gets `team.users.self_update`\\r\\n'\n            '  only — every signed-in operator user can update their own profile\\r\\n'\n            '  from the My Account surface, regardless of other team-management\\r\\n'\n            '  authority.\\r\\n'\n            '- `team_admin` (v2 roster/role-admin role) gets the team-administration\\r\\n'\n            '  subset: `team.users.view`, `team.users.invite`,\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.users.deactivate`, `team.users.reactivate`,\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.users.reset_password`, `team.users.reset_mfa`,\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.users.self_update`, `team.roles.view`, `team.roles.assign`,\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.roles.revoke`, `team.audit_log.view`,\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.session.force_logout`.\\r\\n'\n            '- `finance_analyst` and `training_lead` get `team.users.self_update`\\r\\n'\n            '  only. `auditor_compliance` adds `team.audit_log.view` /\\r\\n'\n            '  `team.audit_log.export` on top of `team.users.self_update` for\\r\\n'\n            '  read-only audit oversight.\\r\\n'\n            '- `team.roles.default_catalog.view` is granted to `super_admin` and\\r\\n'\n            '  `ff_support` only — the F&F-internal Default Role Catalog admin\\r\\n'\n            '  surface (`default_role_catalog_admin_screen.dart`) is the only\\r\\n'\n            '  consumer. Operator-tier roles never receive the grant by default\\r\\n'\n            '  because the default catalog template is global to the F&F\\r\\n'\n            '  deployment.\\r\\n'\n            '- `team.roles.default_catalog.edit` is granted to `super_admin` ONLY.\\r\\n'\n            '  Publishing a new default catalog version affects every operator in\\r\\n'\n            '  the F&F deployment, so the write gate is F&F super-admin-only by\\r\\n'\n            '  design. `ff_support` lands on the read-only branch via the view\\r\\n'\n            '  grant above. Do NOT widen this grant to `operator_owner` or any\\r\\n'\n            '  other operator-scoped role.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '### `account.*` (1)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Operator business-account settings. `account.configure` gates writes to\\r\\n'\n            'the Operator Web Account screen for business identity, region, business\\r\\n'\n            'week, rollover-hour, and logo settings. Grant intent is senior\\r\\n'\n            'operator ownership: `operator_owner` configures the account (this\\r\\n'\n            'includes the account-configuration capability a separate\\r\\n'\n            '`operator_admin` tier was previously described as holding — no such\\r\\n'\n            'seeded role exists; it is part of `operator_owner`); GM-tier and\\r\\n'\n            'below remain read-only.\\r\\n'\n            '`super_admin` is granted explicitly so the seeded super-admin role keeps\\r\\n'\n            'the \"every catalog key\" invariant. No MFA is required at the catalog\\r\\n'\n            'level; route-level freshness can be added later without changing the\\r\\n'\n            'grantable key.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Key | Description | MFA |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `account.configure` | Configure operator business account identity, locale, currency, business-week, rollover-hour, and logo settings. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '### `business_timing.*` (1)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Operator business-timing settings. `business_timing.configure` gates\\r\\n'\n            'writes to the Operator Web Business setup and Business timing editor\\r\\n'\n            'screens. Grant intent mirrors the current operator write route and\\r\\n'\n            'screen posture: `operator_owner` owns timing configuration (the\\r\\n'\n            'timing-configuration capability a separate `operator_admin` tier was\\r\\n'\n            'previously described as holding is part of `operator_owner` — no such\\r\\n'\n            'seeded role exists); GM-tier and below do not receive the default\\r\\n'\n            'grant. `super_admin` is granted explicitly for catalog completeness.\\r\\n'\n            'No MFA is required at the catalog level; closed-day timing authority\\r\\n'\n            'and write validation stay in the business-timing route/service layer.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Key | Description | MFA |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `business_timing.configure` | Configure effective-dated business timing profiles, rollover-hour, week-start, and service periods. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '### `billing.*` (5)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Operator billing actions. All money-moving keys require MFA.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Key | Description | MFA |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `billing.invoice.view` | View operator invoices. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `billing.subscription.manage` | Manage subscription tier + payment terms. | yes |\\r\\n'\n            '| `billing.payment_method.manage` | Add or remove operator payment methods. | yes |\\r\\n'\n            '| `billing.usage.view` | View per-class usage and cost rollups. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `billing.usage_caps.edit` | Edit per-class monthly cap. | yes |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '### `integration.*` (9)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Third-party integration management. `integration.key_rotate` is the\\r\\n'\n            'catch-all rotate-secret action used by Phase 11A.4. Vendor-specific\\r\\n'\n            '`*.connect` keys are split per-vendor for finer control.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Key | Description | MFA |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `integration.toast.connect` | Connect or rotate Toast POS credentials. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `integration.toast.view` | View Toast integration status. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `integration.7shifts.connect` | Connect or rotate 7shifts labor credentials. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `integration.7shifts.view` | View 7shifts integration status. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `integration.opentable.connect` | Connect or rotate OpenTable reservation credentials. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `integration.opentable.view` | View OpenTable integration status. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `integration.qbo.connect` | Connect or rotate QuickBooks Online credentials. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `integration.xero.connect` | Connect or rotate Xero credentials. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `integration.key_rotate` | Rotate any integration secret. | yes |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '### `integrations.*` (1)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Phase 8.0 single-category gate for the Vendor Connections admin\\r\\n'\n            'surface (POS / labor / reservation). Distinct from the per-vendor\\r\\n'\n            '`integration.*` keys above which gate F&F-internal provider-key\\r\\n'\n            'rotation in 11A.4. Granted to `forge_admin` and the senior\\r\\n'\n            'operator role `operator_owner` (which subsumes the integrations\\r\\n'\n            'configuration capability a separate `operator_admin` tier was\\r\\n'\n            'previously described as holding — no such seeded role exists);\\r\\n'\n            'read-only for `ff_support` (no mutate routes wired); denied to\\r\\n'\n            '`location_manager` because misconfigured vendor credentials cascade\\r\\n'\n            'into broken cost / labor data and senior roles own that risk.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Key | Description | MFA |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `integrations.configure` | Configure inbound vendor connections (POS / labor / reservation) on the per-(operator, location) Vendor Connections admin surface. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '### `workflow.*` (8 placeholder)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Phase 12 workflow capabilities. Seeded as placeholder keys so Phase 12\\r\\n'\n            'slices can grant them without another permission-catalog migration.\\r\\n'\n            'None require MFA at the catalog level; Phase 12 may add per-workflow\\r\\n'\n            'MFA-required gates outside the permission catalog.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Key | Description | MFA |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `workflow.catalog.view` | View Phase 12 workflow catalog. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `workflow.run` | Run a Phase 12 workflow. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `workflow.approve` | Approve a Phase 12 workflow approval gate. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `workflow.reject` | Reject a Phase 12 workflow approval gate. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `workflow.create` | Create a Phase 12 workflow. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `workflow.delete` | Delete a Phase 12 workflow. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `workflow.history.view` | View Phase 12 workflow run history. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '| `workflow.tool.invoke` | Invoke a Phase 12 workflow tool directly. | — |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '## Baseline Roles (seeded)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'The seeded role catalog is the **v2 default role catalog** — **ten**\\r\\n'\n            'roles seeded into `public.roles`, all global (`operator_id IS NULL`)\\r\\n'\n            'and `is_seeded = true`. Source of truth:\\r\\n'\n            '`db/migrations/202605150000_phase_r2l_default_role_catalog_v2.sql`\\r\\n'\n            '(operator-approved 2026-05-14; locks role keys, scopes, descriptions,\\r\\n'\n            'MFA gating, and the v1→v2 migration mapping). Custom operator-scoped\\r\\n'\n            'roles are created at runtime via 9.6\\'s POST `/v1/admin/auth/roles`.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '> **History — v1 6-role catalog superseded by v2 (2026-05-14).** This\\r\\n'\n            '> section formerly listed a 6-role v1 catalog\\r\\n'\n            '> (`super_admin`, `ff_support`, `operator_owner`, `operator_manager`,\\r\\n'\n            '> `operator_supervisor`, `operator_staff`). The v1 roles\\r\\n'\n            '> `operator_manager` / `operator_supervisor` / `operator_staff` are\\r\\n'\n            '> **retired / superseded** (soft-deleted, `deleted_at` set, not\\r\\n'\n            '> hard-deleted — the audit trail and FK references are preserved). v2\\r\\n'\n            '> auto-migrates existing grants:\\r\\n'\n            '> `operator_manager → operator_general_manager` (operator-wide);\\r\\n'\n            '> `operator_supervisor → supervisor` (location-scoped, name\\r\\n'\n            '> continuity); `operator_staff → supervisor` (location-scoped,\\r\\n'\n            '> Barrio-only users folded into the shift-supervisor role). A separate\\r\\n'\n            '> `operator_admin` role was **never seeded in v1 or v2** — references\\r\\n'\n            '> to an `operator_admin` \"(when seeded)\" tier elsewhere in this doc\\r\\n'\n            '> have been corrected; that capability is part of `operator_owner`.\\r\\n'\n            '> Readers tracing old `operator_manager` / `operator_supervisor` /\\r\\n'\n            '> `operator_staff` references should map them per the table below.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Role key | `is_editable` | Scope | Intent |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `super_admin` | false | global | F&F company. Every key in the catalog. BYPASSRLS via `forge_admin` Postgres role. |\\r\\n'\n            '| `ff_support` | false | global | F&F support. Read-only across products + admin views; scoped to assigned operators. |\\r\\n'\n            '| `operator_owner` | true | Business | Owns the business. Full operational access plus billing, integrations, and team admin. (Display name `Owner`. Carry-over from v1; also subsumes the never-seeded `operator_admin` tier\\'s capabilities.) |\\r\\n'\n            '| `operator_general_manager` | true | Business | Runs all locations and staff. Operational edit access plus staff admin and audit view; no billing or subscription mutations. (Display name `General Manager`. v2 successor of the retired `operator_manager`.) |\\r\\n'\n            '| `location_manager` | true | Location | Runs one location. Invites and removes staff, edits schedules, sees variance and benchmarks at that location. (Display name `Location Manager`. New v2 role; no v1 antecedent.) |\\r\\n'\n            '| `supervisor` | true | Location | Supervises shifts at one location. Edits short-term schedule, marks shift covers, sees variance for shifts they ran. (Display name `Supervisor`. v2 successor of the retired `operator_supervisor` and `operator_staff`.) |\\r\\n'\n            '| `finance_analyst` | true | Business | Reviews invoices and usage, adjusts usage caps. Cannot change the subscription plan or connect billing integrations. (Display name `Finance Analyst`. New v2 role; no v1 antecedent.) |\\r\\n'\n            '| `auditor_compliance` | true | Business | Read-only audit trail and PII oversight. Sees who did what and when, exports the audit log, cannot mutate data. (Display name `Auditor / Compliance`. New v2 role; no v1 antecedent.) |\\r\\n'\n            '| `training_lead` | true | Either | Manages employee training and onboarding content. Edits supervisor content and the interview playbook; does not edit the F&F handbook source. (Display name `Training Lead`. New v2 role; no v1 antecedent.) |\\r\\n'\n            '| `team_admin` | true | Either | Manages the team roster, role assignments, MFA, and password resets. Does not see operational dashboards. (Display name `Team Admin`. New v2 role; no v1 antecedent.) |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '**Retired v1 roles (superseded — kept soft-deleted for the audit\\r\\n'\n            'trail; do NOT silently drop references):**\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '| Retired v1 role key | Superseded by (v2) | Migration |\\r\\n'\n            '|---|---|---|\\r\\n'\n            '| `operator_manager` | `operator_general_manager` | Auto-migrated operator-wide; v1 row soft-deleted (`deleted_at` set), display name suffixed `(retired)`. |\\r\\n'\n            '| `operator_supervisor` | `supervisor` | Auto-migrated location-scoped (location continuity preserved); v1 row soft-deleted. |\\r\\n'\n            '| `operator_staff` | `supervisor` | Auto-migrated location-scoped (Barrio-only users folded into shift-supervisor); v1 row soft-deleted. |\\r\\n'\n            '| `operator_admin` *(phantom — never seeded)* | `operator_owner` | Never a real seeded role in v1 or v2. Any prior \"(when seeded)\" prose was speculative; the described capabilities are part of `operator_owner`. |\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'The `is_editable` flag protects `super_admin` and `ff_support` from\\r\\n'\n            'runtime grant edits; only super_admin can edit `super_admin` /\\r\\n'\n            '`ff_support` permissions, and that path requires\\r\\n'\n            '`admin.roles.edit_seeded` (MFA-required).\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '## Resolution semantics (preview, lands in 9.6)\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Phase 9.6 implements the runtime resolver. The semantics are:\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '```\\r\\n'\n            'for each user_roles row WHERE user_id = X\\r\\n'\n            '  AND now() BETWEEN valid_from AND COALESCE(valid_until, \\'infinity\\')\\r\\n'\n            '  AND revoked_at IS NULL:\\r\\n'\n            '  join role_permissions\\r\\n'\n            '  collect (permission_key, effect) tuples\\r\\n'\n            'if any (permission_key, \\'deny\\') exists for permission_key, effect = deny\\r\\n'\n            'else if any (permission_key, \\'allow\\') exists, effect = allow\\r\\n'\n            'else effect = deny (default)\\r\\n'\n            '```\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Deny wins. Default deny. The `users.roles_version` column is the cache\\r\\n'\n            'invalidation key; bumping it on any role change drops the entry from\\r\\n'\n            'the JWT custom-claim cache and the in-process permission cache.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '## B5.b catalog reconciliation\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'Surfaced by the 2026-05-06 CODE_HEALTH audit; flagged again by Wave 5\\r\\n'\n            'W5-PKEYS ([#362](https://github.com/SaidKhan005/forge-flow-demo/pull/362))\\r\\n'\n            'during the operator-web permission-key sweep. Historical context:\\r\\n'\n            '`docs/archive/code_health/CODE_HEALTH_2026-05-06_remediation.md`.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'The B5.b follow-up resolves the two operator-web settings namespaces\\r\\n'\n            'that were previously flagged as pending additions:\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '- `lib/operator_web/screens/account_screen.dart` gates on\\r\\n'\n            '  `PermissionKeys.accountConfigure`.\\r\\n'\n            '- `lib/operator_web/screens/business_setup_screen.dart` gates on\\r\\n'\n            '  `PermissionKeys.businessTimingConfigure`.\\r\\n'\n            '- `lib/operator_web/screens/business_timing_editor_screen.dart` gates on\\r\\n'\n            '  `PermissionKeys.businessTimingConfigure`.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            'The catalog rows above, `lib/auth/permission_keys.dart`, and the\\r\\n'\n            'additive B5.b seed migration are the coordinated mirrors for these two\\r\\n'\n            'keys. No B2/B10 admin keys were added.\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '## Out of catalog scope\\r\\n'\n            '\\r\\n'\n            '- Vendor-specific operator-scoped permissions (e.g., overriding a\\r\\n'\n            '  third-party integration credential at row level) are handled by\\r\\n'\n            '  RLS, not the catalog.\\r\\n'\n            '- Time-bound and location-scoped grants are dimensions of `user_roles`,\\r\\n'\n            '  not the catalog. The catalog defines what is grantable; `user_roles`\\r\\n'\n            '  defines who, where, and for how long.\\r\\n'\n            '- Step-up MFA challenges beyond `requires_mfa` (e.g., re-prompt after\\r\\n'\n            '  N minutes of inactivity) are session policy, not catalog.\\r\\n'\n            ''\n   Which: does not contain '`operator_owner` and `operator_admin`'\n","stackTrace":"package:matcher                                     expect\npackage:flutter_test/src/widget_tester.dart 473:18  expect\ntest\\auth\\permission_catalog_b5b_test.dart 48:7     main.<fn>.<fn>\n","isFailure":true,"type":"error","time":114539}
